whitepaper(anchor): add four-phases, verification-stack, revocation-gossip figures

Three new figures for the Anchor Protocol paper:

- fig-anchor-four-phases.tex (replaces 3-phase predecessor at section 2 head):
  each phase as a labeled card with primitive in the header, property in the
  body, the threat it forecloses in a cinnabar callout, and a patina "needs"
  rationale pill on the arrow into the next phase. Bottom band carries the
  ProVerif mechanization status across all four phases.

- fig-anchor-verification-stack.tex (new at section 4 head): three-layer
  stack (ProVerif symbolic / Kani bounded model checking on harbor-card-rs /
  runtime conformance on the deployed binary). Cinnabar down-arrows carry
  design obligations; patina up-arrows carry implementation evidence. Bridge
  labels make the specification-gap and deployment-gap closures explicit.

- fig-anchor-revocation-gossip.tex (new at section 2.4, downstream of the
  cuckoo mechanics figure): five-panel time series (t = 0, 30s, 60s, 90s,
  120s) tracing a single revocation across a 5-daemon mesh via anti-entropy
  gossip. Version-vector labels per panel; legend and mechanism band below.

All three follow the Harbor Heritage palette and the flat-blueprint TikZ
voice. Every figure is wrapped in resizebox(textwidth, !). PDF rebuilt
three passes; paper grows from 22 to 23 pages.


